# {{app_name}}

A full-stack app on **Cloudflare** (Workers + Containers) with **Neon** Postgres,
scaffolded by `akm`.

## Stack

- **Frontend:** React + Vite → static assets served by a Worker.
- **Backend:** FastAPI in a Cloudflare Container (managed by a Durable Object).
- **DB:** Neon Serverless Postgres (pooled endpoint for traffic, direct for migrations).
- **Auth:** Cloudflare Access → the Worker validates the Access JWT and mints an
  internal `X-Akm-Identity` the backend trusts.

## Layout

```
src/worker/      Worker entry, Container DO, Access→identity auth
src/{{app_pkg}}/backend/   FastAPI app, Neon engine, identity validation
ui/              React frontend
migrations/      Alembic (direct endpoint)
wrangler.jsonc   Cloudflare config (containers + DO + assets)
Dockerfile       Backend container image (linux/amd64)
```

## Develop

`akm dev` runs the whole app on **one origin** for local development. It starts
uvicorn (FastAPI, `--reload`) and the Vite dev server, then fronts both with a
reverse proxy: `/api/*` goes to the backend, everything else to Vite. On every
`/api` request the proxy strips client identity headers and injects a freshly
minted `X-Akm-Identity` — the *same* assertion the prod Worker mints — so the
backend's auth path is identical locally and in production.

Prerequisites: [`uv`](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) and `npm`. First time:

```bash
uv sync                       # backend deps
npm install                   # UI + wrangler deps
cp .dev.vars.example .dev.vars   # set DATABASE_URL / DATABASE_URL_DIRECT
akm dev                       # → http://localhost:8787
```

`akm dev` reads `.dev.vars` for `DATABASE_URL*` and `AKM_INTERNAL_JWT_KEY`
(if the key is absent, an ephemeral one is generated for the session and shared
with the backend). HMR works through the proxy; edits to `ui/` reload live.

| Flag | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `[dir]` | `.` | Project directory |
| `--port N` | `8787` | Proxy (the URL you open) |
| `--backend-port N` | `8000` | uvicorn |
| `--vite-port N` | `5173` | Vite |
| `--dev-user EMAIL` | `dev@akm.local` | Identity injected on `/api/*` |
| `--neon-branch` | off | Create an ephemeral Neon branch for the session (deleted on exit) |
| `--neon-project ID` | — | Neon project for `--neon-branch` (or `NEON_PROJECT_ID`) |

```bash
# Run against a throwaway Neon dev branch (needs neonctl auth):
akm dev --neon-branch --neon-project <project-id>
```

Quick check once it's up:

```bash
curl localhost:8787/api/health   # {"status":"ok"}
curl localhost:8787/api/me       # echoes the injected dev identity
```

### UI components (shadcn/ui)

```bash
akm components init              # one-time: Tailwind v4 + cn util + @/ alias
akm components add button card   # fetch components into ui/components/ui/
```

`components add` pulls from the shadcn registry over HTTPS, writes the files, and
installs their npm deps. Import them with the `@/` alias, e.g.
`import { Button } from "@/components/ui/button"`.

## Deploy

Prerequisites: a **Workers Paid** plan (Containers aren't on the free tier), local
**Docker** running, a Neon project, `npm install` done, and `wrangler login`.

Put your production secrets in a `.prod.vars` file (same `KEY="value"` format as
`.dev.vars`, and **gitignored** — never commit it):

```bash
# .prod.vars
AKM_INTERNAL_JWT_KEY="…"          # same value the Worker + container share
DATABASE_URL="…-pooler…"           # Neon pooled endpoint (app traffic)
DATABASE_URL_DIRECT="…"            # Neon direct endpoint (migrations)
CF_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN="myteam"
CF_ACCESS_AUD="…"
```

Validate everything without deploying (no account/Docker needed):

```bash
akm deploy --dry-run               # build + validate wrangler config & bundle
```

Then deploy — `akm deploy` builds artifacts, uploads the secrets atomically
(`wrangler secret bulk`), and runs `wrangler deploy` (which builds the container
image and deploys the Worker / Durable Object / assets):

```bash
akm deploy --secrets .prod.vars --migrate
#   --migrate        run `alembic upgrade head` over DATABASE_URL_DIRECT first
#   --env NAME       target a named wrangler environment (define it in wrangler.jsonc)
#   --skip-build     deploy already-built artifacts
```

> Prefer raw tooling? `npm run build` then `wrangler secret put …` + `wrangler deploy`
> still work. See the project `goal.md` for the full architecture and rationale.

### Preview deploys (per PR)

Each PR gets an isolated **named Worker** (`{{app_slug}}-pr-<id>`) plus its own
**ephemeral Neon branch** (`akm-pr-<id>`). Container/DO Workers don't get native
Wrangler preview URLs (goal.md §5), so this uses a named deploy rather than a preview URL.
Wire these into CI (PR opened / closed):

```bash
akm preview create  --pr 123 --neon-project <id> --secrets .prod.vars   # on open/update
akm preview destroy --pr 123 --neon-project <id>                        # on close/merge
```

`create` makes/reuses the Neon branch, injects its DB URLs as the Worker's secrets
(other secrets come from `--secrets`), and deploys; `destroy` deletes the Worker and the
branch. Add `--dry-run` to validate without deploying.
